# relay-drivers.slice - OS-056 (Milo): the cgroup slice for relay driver
# processes.
#
# Driver processes are first-class citizens of the system, identical in
# standing to relay-worker@ instances (plan/META_OS.md, driver section):
# each driver runs as a systemd unit in this slice, under the OS-034
# supervision contract (systemd owns process death; the watchdog owns
# silent-but-alive stalls) and under per-process cgroup limits.
#
# The slice is separate from relay-workers.slice on purpose: a runaway
# driver must not eat the worker slice budget, and a runaway worker
# must not starve the drivers. Both slices share the OS-035 starting
# defaults until driver profiles are measured:
#   CPUQuota=100%  one CPU-equivalent per driver, so a wedged driver
#                  cannot take every CPU the bus, queue, and
#                  dashboard need on a small multi-CPU machine.
#   MemoryMax=1G   a runaway leak is capped before it threatens the box.
#
# Wiring: the per-driver template unit (one instance per driver, the
# driver runner program itself is not landed yet) sets
# Slice=relay-drivers.slice. The slice needs no [Install] section:
# systemd creates it on demand when the first driver instance joins
# it, and drops it when the last member leaves.
#
# Basis, stated plainly: the repo load numbers are wall-clock tick
# timings, not driver memory or CPU profiles, so these are
# conservative starting defaults, not tuned measurements. The tuning
# pass against measured driver RSS and CPU on the test image is
# still owed, and it replaces these values here and in META_OS.md
# when it lands.
#
# Honest gaps, same pattern as OS-033 and OS-035: a driver process
# appearing in this slice on a booted test image is NOT proven here.
# There is no test image in this repo, no driver runner program
# exists yet for a template unit to start, and this dev VM exposes
# no cpu or memory cgroup controller, so live enforcement cannot
# run here. The drill intel/drills/driver_supervision.py checks
# this file and systemd-analyze verify, then proves the other half
# of OS-056 that fixtures can prove: driver heartbeats feed the
# existing WDG stall detectors unchanged (a driver nick gone from
# presence with a claimed job yields exactly the same
# presence-stall alert a worker would, and the tick never mutates
# the job, so systemd alone owns any restart).
[Unit]
Description=Meta OS relay driver slice
Before=slices.target

[Slice]
CPUQuota=100%
MemoryMax=1G
